  "final_text": "The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. I haven't opened the dashboard or checked that the rule's query matches any documents.\n\n**Data:** The data view is web server logs with a `timestamp` time field. The fields that matter here are `response` (a string, so I used `response.keyword`), `extension`, `bytes`, `clientip`, `host`, `geo.src`, `geo.dest`, `machine.os`, `request`, `url` and `agent`.\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-ff54b147 Web logs overview\" has four panels:\n- Total requests (single number).\n- Requests over time (line chart).\n- Requests by response code (pie chart).\n- Average bytes by file extension (bar chart).\n\nYou can open it at http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-ff54b147-web-logs-overview-370502ce492c.\n\n**Alert rule:** \"EFF-ff54b147 5xx spike\" runs every minute. It fires when more than 10 documents in the last 5 minutes have a `response.keyword` matching `5xx` (regex `5[0-9][0-9]`).\n\nThe rule was created disabled, so I enabled it in a second step. The sample data's timestamps are shifted relative to when it was loaded. If the data isn't being refreshed, the 5-minute window may never contain recent documents, and the rule may not fire.",
